Examples:

- project library / recent projects;
- Capture Inbox before promotion;
- shared/reference libraries;
- activity/jobs;
- support/diagnostics;
- preferences/data management.

These can exist when no project is open.

They must not be disguised as project-local Room/Measurement pages.

### B. Project primary workflow

Keep the high-frequency theater workflow compact.

Current candidates remain valuable:

- Overview;
- Room;
- Measurements;
- Optimize.

The review does **not** require replacing these names.

### C. Project secondary domains

Examples may include:

- Equipment/System;
- Install/Commission;
- Video;
- Reports/Deliverables.

Do not automatically make every domain a permanent rail item.

Choose explicit rules for when a secondary domain is:

- a project hub;
- a context page inside an existing hub;
- a deep-linked task surface;
- a modal/inspector;
- application scope instead.

Document the rule.

