Deep video-commissioning review of HTDT `main@6ad227fafc88c6f19e0bdda927114326e2d5a081` found that #557 intentionally stops at photometric/HDR luminance/contrast and explicitly leaves full color calibration out of scope.

Repository/issue search found no separate authority/workflow for measured:
- white point / grayscale balance;
- chromaticity;
- color gamut coverage/accuracy;
- color error metrics;
- EOTF/grayscale tracking beyond simple peak luminance;
- meter correction/profile provenance;
- pattern-generator/source-chain conditions.

This leaves the video twin unable to record an ordinary commissioning result such as:

> Projector Movie mode was measured after installation: grayscale/EOTF is within the selected project tolerance, gamut points are measured, and the exact meter/pattern/source condition is retained.

## Goal

Add a bounded **Video Colorimetry / Calibration Verification** authority.

Initial scope is measurement, interpretation, comparison and verification.

Do **not** require:
- automated display controls;
- 1D/3D LUT generation;
- vendor DDC integration;
