## 1. Separate target, measurement and applied calibration

Keep distinct:

### VideoColorTargetProfile
> Desired/reference colorimetric behavior for one playback condition.

### VideoColorMeasurementSet
> Observed meter readings under one exact measurement condition.

### VideoColorEvaluation
> Comparison of one measurement set to one exact target profile using one exact metric/algorithm version.

### Applied display/projector calibration state
> Picture mode/CMS/white-balance/LUT/device setting state actually in use.

Do not make a good measurement result proof that settings were applied by HTDT.

## 2. Target profile

Versioned target profile may define:
- transfer-function/EOTF reference;
- reference white point;
- primary/secondary chromaticity targets;
- luminance/reference-level target where #557 provides authority;
- grayscale stimulus points;
- gamut test points;
- optional color-checker/test-patch set;
- tolerance policy;
- source/standard provenance.

Target profiles should be reusable project/reference authorities.

Do not hard-code one universal `correct` profile for all SDR/HDR modes.

## 3. Measurement samples

Represent exact measured tristimulus/chromaticity data with enough primitive authority to recompute metrics.

Preferred canonical sample contains quantities such as:
- stimulus/test-patch identity;
- measured XYZ or another explicit canonical tristimulus representation;
- luminance where available;
- measurement timestamp/order;
- meter/instrument ref;
- measurement status/quality.

Derived xy/uv/DeltaE values should be recomputable from canonical samples + algorithm.

Do not persist only screenshots or final pass/fail numbers.

## 4. Stimulus definition

Every measurement set must identify what was displayed.

Examples:
- grayscale code value / stimulus percentage;
- primary/secondary patch;
- saturation sweep point;
- color-checker patch;
- HDR metadata/test pattern condition.

Store:
- signal encoding/range where known;
- bit depth where relevant;
- patch size / window/APL condition when relevant to display behavior;
- pattern generator/source identity;
- playback path.

Do not compare measurements from materially different stimulus conditions as if identical.

## 5. Projection vs direct view

Compose with #557/#637.

### Projection
Measurement condition may include:
- projector operating mode;
- laser/lamp level;
- iris;
- exact VideoPresentationProfile #565;
- screen authority;
- measurement position/geometry;
- theater LightingScene #640;
- ambient condition.

### Direct view
Measurement condition may include:
- display picture mode;
- brightness/backlight/OLED level;
- local-dimming state;
- window/APL pattern condition;
- ambient/bias-light

