## Summary

Static review of current HTDT main found that the workflow-first Windows UI is effectively hard-coded Japanese rather than localized through a shared presentation layer.

Representative current files:
- workflow_shell.py: Japanese literals present, no Qt translation API use found.
- room_workspace.py: hundreds of Japanese characters/literals, no translation API use found.
- measurement_page_workspace.py: extensive Japanese labels/status text, no translation API use found.
- optimization_workflow_workspace.py: extensive Japanese labels/status text, no translation API use found.
