## Why this matters

A home theater is not only an acoustic system.

Typical real configurations include:

source device
-> AVR / processor / switch
-> projector / display

plus possible return paths:

display
-> eARC/ARC
-> AVR

and alternate paths for:

- game console;
- streaming device;
- UHD player;
- PC;
- low-latency direct-to-display routing.

A system may be acoustically and geometrically correct while the intended video/audio mode is impossible or unreliable through the selected signal chain.

## Proposed authority

Add an immutable/versioned AVSignalPath / MediaSignalRoute authority.

It should bind exact physical/device instances where available (#569), and otherwise exact equipment definitions/project entities.

### 1. Nodes and ports

Represent relevant endpoints/ports such as:

- source output;
- AVR/processer input/output;
- HDMI switch/splitter;
- projector/display input;
- eARC/ARC endpoint;
- optional network/media endpoint where explicitly modeled.

Do not require detailed connector geometry.

Port identity and capability are enough for MVP.

### 2. Edges

An edge references:

- source port;
- destination port;
- connection medium/type;
- optional CableRun (#538);
- known cable/adapter capability;
- evidence/provenance.

Examples:

- HDMI;
- eARC/ARC;
- analog audio;
- optical/coax digital;
- USB audio;
- network media/control where useful.

Do not claim protocol behavior merely because a cable type label exists.

## Capability contract

Use explicit versioned capability sets.

Candidate video capabilities:

- resolution;
- refresh rate;
- pixel format/chroma;
- bit depth;
- HDR transfer/format family where supported;
- VRR/ALLM-like feature flags when explicitly documented;
- bandwidth/rate class only when sourced.

Candidate audio transport capabilities:

- PCM channel counts/sample rates;
- compressed bitstream families where explicitly documented;
- ARC/eARC mode;
- object-audio passthrough capability when supported by source/device evidence.

Do not build a proprietary decoder implementation.

## Compatibility evaluation

Given an exact requested MediaPlaybackCondition, evaluate path capability by intersection of supported documented node/edge capabilities.

Return explicit states:

- SUPPORTED by documented capability;
- UNSUPPORTED by a known limiting capability;
- UNKNOWN because a device/cable/adapter capability is missing;
- VERIFIED_WORKING from explicit field evidence;
- VERIFIED_FAILURE from explicit field evidence.

A documented capability intersection is not proof that a real HDMI/HDCP/EDID handshake will succeed.

## Handshake / protected-protocol boundary

Do not claim deterministic HDMI/HDCP/EDID behavior from static specs alone.

