## Summary

Deep product/spec review of current `main@6a463b6fa4f4bd85ac3a944938004f6a9cfc80e3` found a missing target-authority layer.

HTDT has:

- `TargetCurveProfile` direction for frequency-response/EQ targets (#508);
- `StandardsProfile` for traceable compliance criteria (#170);
- solver plans/results for RT60, EDT, C50/C80, reflection/decay metrics (#101);
- treatment optimization planning that may use decay and early-energy objectives (#516);
- a new project-level Design Brief issue (#555).

But there is no first-class **user/project acoustic performance target profile** for time-domain/decay/spatial goals.

## Why existing authorities are not enough

### TargetCurveProfile

A frequency-response target does not define:

- desired EDT/T20/T30 by band;
- allowed decay variation;
- early reflection / early energy intent;
- clarity targets;
- seat-to-seat consistency goals;
- frequency-dependent decay envelopes.

### StandardsProfile

Compliance is not acoustic optimality.

A user may intentionally choose project goals that are:

- stricter than one standard;
- looser in one band;
- not defined by a published standard at all.

StandardsProfile should be able to evaluate a project target where appropriate, but should not be the only place the target exists.

## Proposed authority

Add an immutable/versioned `AcousticPerformanceTargetProfile` (name flexible).

Candidate criterion types:

- decay-time target/range by explicit frequency band;
- EDT/T20/T30 target semantics, kept distinct;
- early/late energy metrics where solver/measurement capability exists;
- C50/C80 or similar metrics where appropriate;
- seat-to-seat spread/envelope targets;
- early-reflection/path constraints;
- optional room-noise target references through #532;
- explicit valid population/seat set.

Each criterion should retain:

- metric definition/version;
- frequency domain/bands;
- desired range/target;
- aggregation semantics;
- required capability;
- project/user/source provenance;
- whether it is hard constraint, optimization objective, or informational.

Do not create one overall acoustic score.

## Capability boundary

A target existing does not mean the current provider can evaluate it.

Examples:

- measured T30 exists, but hypothetical treatment candidates cannot be scored on T30 until a prediction authority supports compatible decay output;
- FR-only prediction cannot claim C80;
- magnitude-only evidence cannot invent time-domain metrics.

Evaluation result must support explicit:

- AVAILABLE;
- UNKNOWN/UNSUPPORTED;
- BLOCKED;

with reasons.

## Workflow

### Project / Overview

Allow selection from #555 ProjectDesignBrief.

Show which target criteria are currently:

- evaluable from prediction;
- evaluable from measured evidence only;
- blocked by missing capability/evidence.

### Prediction / Measurements

Display exact result vs exact target profile, while preserving predicted/measured distinction.

### Optimize

Objectives/constraints should bind the exact target/profile version.

Changing the target profile stales/revises dependent optimization results but does not rewrite historical runs.

### Treatment

#516 should reuse the same target authority rather than embedding anonymous decay goals in a treatment-only SearchSpec.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] User can define versioned non-FR acoustic performance goals.
- [ ] EDT/T20/T30 are not treated as interchangeable labels.
- [ ] Frequency bands and aggregation/population semantics are explicit.
- [ ] Predicted and measured evaluation remain distinct.
- [ ] Unsupported metrics return explicit unavailable/unknown state.
- [ ] Optimize/treatment workflows can bind an exact target-profile version.
- [ ] Changing targets does not rewrite historical comparisons/optimization.
- [ ] StandardsProfile can reference/evaluate compatible targets without owning user intent.
- [ ] ProjectDesignBrief can reference the exact profile.
- [ ] No hidden overall room-quality score is introduced.
- [ ] RDC 0

## Summary

HTDT already has projector/screen/sightline geometry authority (#175) and an open native UX gap (#455), but #175 explicitly excluded full SDR/HDR color calibration and the current product has no first-class **photometric/video commissioning authority**.

For a Home Theater Digital Twin, geometry alone answers "will the image fit and be visible?" but not "will the installed projector/screen combination deliver the intended image luminance/contrast under the actual room conditions?"

Review basis: `main@6a463b6fa4f4bd85ac3a944938004f6a9cfc80e3`.

## Scope for a bounded first slice

This issue does **not** need to become a full color-management suite.

Start with evidence/provenance-correct photometric commissioning:

- projector light-output specification by operating mode, with manufacturer/user/measured provenance;
- screen gain and gain provenance, optionally angle-dependent when exact data exists;
- visible image area from existing video geometry authority;
- lens/throw/light-loss factors only when explicit supported data exists;
- ambient-light / room-light observation or measurement;
- measured on-screen luminance from a photometer/colorimeter import/manual record;
- black-floor / contrast measurement when available;
- SDR/HDR target profiles as versioned references, with UNKNOWN when required evidence is missing;
- exact projector mode / laser-lamp level / iris state used for measurement.

Derived quantities may include expected/measured screen luminance and contrast, but must retain inputs/provenance and avoid false precision.

## Why this matters

Two layouts can both pass throw ratio and sightline checks while differing substantially in usable image brightness because of:

- screen size;
- screen gain;
- projector mode;
- throw/lens configuration;
- ambient light;
- projector aging/output state.

The current digital twin therefore stops before a major real-world acceptance question.

## Workflow

### Room / Equipment

Bind projector and screen photometric capability data to exact equipment definitions.

### Design comparison

Show independent video criteria per alternative:

- geometry/sightline status from existing authority;
- expected photometric status;
- measured commissioning status.

Do not produce a hidden overall theater score.

### Commissioning

Allow import/manual entry of measured luminance/contrast evidence and bind it to:

- exact SceneRevision/SystemVariant;
- projector/screen equipment;
- operating state;
- measurement instrument/calibration;
- projector mode/settings;
- timestamp.

### Validation

Keep predicted/manufacturer-derived and measured values separate.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Projector/screen photometric inputs have explicit provenance and versioned identity.
- [ ] Screen area reuses exact video geometry rather than duplicating dimensions.
- [ ] Expected luminance can be evaluated only when required inputs are supported.
- [ ] Measured luminance/contrast evidence is stored separately from prediction.
- [ ] Projector operating mode/settings used for commissioning are exact inputs.
- [ ] SDR/HDR target/reference profiles are versioned and source-attributed.
- [ ] Missing screen gain/output/ambient-light evidence yields UNKNOWN, not a guessed PASS.
- [ ] Variant comparison can present geometry and photometric criteria independently.
- [ ] Reports can include design vs measured video commissioning results.
- [ ] Full CMS/3D-LUT generation remains out of scope unless separately planned.

