## Summary

Cross-repository review found a lifecycle mismatch: HTDT-Capture already tracks the need for a `RoomStateSnapshot` in #264, but HTDT itself has no corresponding first-class operating-state authority that predictions, measurements, comparisons and commissioning can bind.

Review basis: `main@6a463b6fa4f4bd85ac3a944938004f6a9cfc80e3`.

This is distinct from permanent SceneRevision geometry and from SystemVariant proposal/as-built lifecycle.

## Ordinary examples

A physically unchanged theater can have materially different acoustic/video behavior depending on:

- door/window open vs closed;
- curtains open vs closed;
- movable acoustic panels deployed/retracted;
- retractable screen or masking state;
- seats upright/reclined where geometry matters;
- removable furniture/treatment present/absent;
- HVAC / ventilation / fan operating state;
- projector operating mode or other state relevant to commissioning.

Today these conditions are liable to become notes, ad-hoc fields or an implicit assumption of "whatever the room looked like then".

## Why this matters

Without exact operating-state identity, HTDT cannot reliably distinguish:

- geometry changed;
- equipment/settings changed;
- same physical room under a different operating configuration.

That weakens:

- predicted-vs-measured validation;
- before/after comparisons;
- owned-room solver validation;
- calibration verification;
- commissioning reports;
- Capture -> HTDT handoff.

A measurement result should be able to say exactly which room operating state was active.

## Proposed authority

Introduce an immutable/versioned `RoomOperatingState` / `RoomStateSnapshot` authority.

It should bind:

- exact project/document and SceneRevision;
- stateful entity/surface references;
- typed state observations;
- observation/effective time;
- source/provenance (user attestation, Capture evidence, device state where supported);
- semantic digest/version;
- optional campaign/task identity.

State observations must not silently rewrite geometry. If a state change materially changes effective geometry/physics, the corresponding solver materialization should be explicit and capability-gated.

## Workflow

### Room

Allow users to define supported movable/stateful elements and named operating snapshots, e.g.:

- "Movie night — curtains closed / HVAC low";
- "Measurement — HVAC off";
- "Day use — curtains open".

### Prediction

Every prediction request that depends on operating state binds an exact snapshot. Unsupported state effects remain UNKNOWN/BLOCKED rather than being ignored.

### Measurements

AcquisitionContext / MeasurementCampaign binds the exact snapshot active for that measurement.

### Compare

Comparison should separate:

- SceneRevision difference;
- SystemVariant/equipment difference;
- operating-state difference.

## Capture integration

Design the HTDT authority so HTDT-Capture #264 can hand off an observed RoomStateSnapshot without inventing a parallel incompatible schema.

Capture observation means "state observed/attested at capture time"; HTDT remains responsible for deciding which state effects are supported by a solver/evaluator.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Multiple immutable operating-state snapshots can exist for one SceneRevision.
- [ ] Measurements/campaigns can bind the exact snapshot used.
- [ ] Prediction requests can bind exact supported state inputs.
- [ ] Changing state invalidates only dependent results through exact identity.
- [ ] UNKNOWN/unrecorded state stays explicit.
- [ ] State changes do not mutate historical SceneRevision or measured evidence.
- [ ] Capture #264 can map deterministically into this authority.
- [ ] Comparison/report UI distinguishes geometry, system/settings and operating-state changes.
- [ ] No RDC is required for the authority/software slice.

