## Current problem

Today the project's design intent is distributed across independent inputs:

- geometry and physical constraints in Room;
- StandardsProfile criteria;
- optimization objectives/SearchSpec;
- target-curve profiles;
- seat-priority semantics;
- topology/headroom/cost criteria;
- projector/sightline evaluation;
- calibration/measurement plans.

Those individual authorities should stay independent, but there is no immutable record answering:

> What is this theater being designed to achieve, for whom, under which explicit constraints and priorities?

As a result, two optimization/commissioning runs can be technically reproducible while still lacking one exact authority describing why their goals differ.

The Overview workspace is primarily readiness-driven; it does not present a project brief against which current/proposed/as-built/measured status can be checked.

## Proposed authority

Add a versioned `ProjectDesignBrief` (name illustrative) bound to a project/document identity.

