## Summary

Deep static Room/product review of current main (79262f50777f61e79d12a3be2afdbbb2d5a2680d) found that HTDT treats every seat as an individually authored SceneEntity.

That is sufficient as a low-level authority, but it creates a large normal-workflow gap for real home-theater layouts:

> users cannot author seat rows / repeated seating layouts from explicit spacing, aisle and riser rules.

This becomes increasingly costly now that downstream HTDT capabilities are explicitly multi-seat:

- sightlines / viewing geometry;
- multi-seat prediction;
- multi-seat measurement analysis;
- measurement campaigns;
