## Why this matters

A realistic layout may contain:

- 2–4 seat rows;
- 3–6 seats per row;
- center or side aisles;
- different row widths;
- riser elevation for rear rows;
- staggered seat centers;
- one MLP/priority seat;
- per-seat listener/eye references.

Creating and positioning every seat independently increases:

- coordinate-entry effort;
- spacing errors;
- accidental asymmetry;
- inconsistent listener-reference placement;
- difficulty changing row spacing later;
- difficulty regenerating comparable alternatives.

A repeated layout should still materialize into individually addressable seats because prediction/measurement evidence binds to exact seat identities.

## Proposed change

Add a first-class **Seating Layout / Seat Row authoring workflow** that generates ordinary SceneEntity seats.

The layout tool is an authoring aid/derived specification; individual seats remain the physical scene authority after materialization.

### 1. Row specification

Allow a row to define at minimum:

- row name/index;
- seat count;
- seat body preset/template;
- center-to-center spacing;
- row center or start/end anchor;
- row direction;
- orientation;
- optional stagger/offset;
- optional riser binding.

All generated coordinates must be deterministic.

### 2. Aisle/gap handling

Support explicit:

- center aisle;
- left/right aisle;
- custom gap after seat N;
- different gap width.

