### 3. Multiple rows

Allow:

- row-to-row spacing;
- shared alignment;
- independent row width/count;
- front/back offset;
- optional alternating stagger.

Rows must not assume the room is rectangular.

### 4. Riser integration

Coordinate with #455.

A row may explicitly bind to one riser/platform.

The tool should show:

- seat base elevation;
- riser top;
- support status;
- sightline impact where the existing evaluator supports it.

Generating seats must not silently generate a riser unless the user explicitly requests one.

### 5. Listener / eye / head references

