Deep product/spec review of current `main` (`e8c5ea042b81e0c475e8a42efa8a25a5bfc14d2d`) found an untracked feature gap that is already explicitly called out in HTDT's competitive-product research.

`docs/COMPETITIVE_PRODUCT_RESEARCH_2026-09-19.md` section **“O. Background-noise / noise-floor performance”** says HTDT should:

- import/measure background noise;
- optionally evaluate NC/NCB-style criteria;
- retain projector/PC/AVR fan-noise notes;
- use measured noise floor to determine usable measurement dynamic range/SNR;
- **not** attempt first-principles HVAC simulation.

Repository/issue search found no dedicated background-noise authority or workflow.

Related: #468, #471, #456/#170 StandardsProfile work, #455, #507

## Existing partial capability

`CadMeasurementQualityEvidence` already contains scalar fields such as:

- `noise_floor_db_spl`;
- `snr_db`.

