## Summary

HTDT can represent the room in 3D and is developing richer arbitrary-room acoustic solvers under #101, but the native product still lacks a first-class **spatial field result** and an interactive way to inspect how a predicted field varies through the room.

This issue defines the authority and UX for field visualization without coupling the UI to one FEM/FDTD/geometric backend.

Related: #101, #118, #457, #469, #492, #479

## Product goal

Allow a user to inspect, for an exact prediction authority:

- XY / XZ / YZ slices;
- arbitrary probe points;
- frequency scrub;
- complex pressure where available;
- SPL/magnitude;
- phase;
- selected modal distributions;
- early/late energy fields where the provider actually supports them;
- seat/region variation.

The field view is a scientific visualization of exact solver output/derived data, not an interpolated decorative heatmap.

## Solver-neutral authority

Introduce a **SpatialFieldResult** contract (name flexible) separate from point-receiver PredictionResult.

Pin:

- exact SceneRevision/SystemVariant;
- exact source/excitation scenario;
- environment authority;
- solver/provider ID/version;
- geometry/material compilation identity;
- valid frequency/time domain;
- coordinate frame/unit;
- sampled domain/grid/mesh identity;
- field quantity and units;
- complex-vs-derived representation;
