- phase;
- energy density or other explicitly defined provider output;
- derived modal magnitude.

Do not expose a quantity simply because the UI can color-map it.

## Storage / cache model

Full 3D multi-frequency field data can be large.

Use a bounded design:

- canonical numerical result may remain provider-native/content-addressed;
- slice/probe products are derived caches;
- request only selected frequencies/regions where possible;
- lazy extraction;
- LOD/downsampling for display;
- cache key includes exact result + slice geometry + quantity + interpolation settings;
- cancellation/stale protection via existing computation-job patterns.

Do not persist every viewport interpolation as new authority.

