## Summary

Static product/UX review of current `main` (`a597c66b4f5902381f370ce6f24ca56bfb737566`) found no general-purpose distance/angle measurement tool in the workflow-first Room editor.

The Inspector can show one selected object's coordinates and dimensions, but the user cannot directly measure arbitrary geometric relationships in the 3D scene.

Related: #118, #455, #481, #486, #453

## Current behavior

The canonical Room workspace provides:

- object Inspector position X/Y/Z;
- object size X/Y/Z;
- room/wall geometry panels;
- move/rotate tools;
- viewport grid.

Static review of:

- `room_workspace.py`;
- `room_viewport.py`;
- `cad_input.py`;
- `room_geometry_panel.py`;

found no ruler/distance/angle measurement interaction.

## Why this matters

Typical home-theater design questions are relational:

- distance from speaker acoustic reference to front/side wall;
- FL ↔ FR separation;
- speaker ↔ MLP distance;
- listener ↔ screen distance;
- projector lens ↔ screen plane throw distance;
- riser/seat spacing;
- aisle width;
- treatment spacing;
- floor/ceiling height difference;
- toe-in/viewing angle.

Users should not need to manually subtract coordinates or create temporary constraints just to inspect these values.

A constraint is a design rule. A ruler measurement is a transient observation. They should remain separate concepts.

## Proposed change

Add a lightweight **Measure** tool to Room.

### 1. Distance

Allow selection of:

- point → point;
- entity acoustic/reference point → point;
- entity center/reference → entity center/reference;
- point → wall/plane nearest point.

Display:

- total 3D distance;
- optional ΔX / ΔY / ΔZ;
- horizontal distance where useful.

### 2. Angle

Support useful angular measurements such as:

- angle between two rays/segments;
- horizontal azimuth;
- vertical elevation;
- angle at a selected listener/reference point.

This can support speaker placement and projector/viewing workflows without becoming Standards authority.

### 3. Snap integration

Measurement endpoints should use the same geometric snap engine introduced by #481:

- vertices;
- edges;
- midpoints;
- acoustic reference points;
- listener references.

Free-point measurement should still be possible.

### 4. Temporary by default

Ruler annotations should be editor/view state and should **not** change SceneRevision by default.

Optional future persistent dimensions/annotations should be a separate explicit feature.

### 5. Semantic reference choice

When an entity has multiple meaningful references, allow the user to choose/see what is being measured:

- body origin;
- acoustic source reference;
- listener/ear reference;
- measurement/capsule point;
- projector lens reference;
- screen plane/center.

Do not silently choose a semantically wrong point.

### 6. Copy/use value

Allow copying the measured numeric value for use in:

- Inspector;
- constraint authoring (#486);
- installation notes/report.

Do not automatically create a hard constraint from a ruler measurement.

## Acceptance

- [ ] user can measure point-to-point distance directly in Room.
- [ ] user can measure entity-reference-to-entity-reference distance.
- [ ] horizontal and vertical component deltas are available.
- [ ] angle/azimuth/elevation can be inspected for useful geometry.
- [ ] measurement endpoints can snap to canonical geometry/reference points.
- [ ] active ruler is visibly distinct from physical Scene geometry and constraints.
- [ ] temporary measurements do not dirty or modify SceneRevision.
- [ ] selected semantic reference type is visible.
