## Finding

Static integration review of current HTDT `main` (`9e6066259ec58c093e9a7587550ccf907f28402f`) and HTDT-Capture `main` (`0b976b98245bcc40a36e34755370130627b7ac4c`) found that the HTDT -> Capture equipment-catalog snapshot contract is implemented independently in both repositories but has no cross-repository compatibility fixture/CI.

HTDT currently provides:

- `EquipmentCatalogSnapshot`;
- deterministic `canonical_bytes()`;
- `CadEquipmentRepository.catalog_snapshot()`;
- `scripts/export_equipment_catalog_snapshot.py`.

HTDT-Capture provides:

- `HTDTEquipmentCatalogSnapshot`;
- `HTDTEquipmentCatalogEntry`;
- UI JSON import;
- unit tests that decode a hand-written JSON string.

The Capture test fixture is not generated by the actual HTDT exporter/model.

## Why this matters

Both repositories can pass independently while the wire contract drifts.

Examples of contract surface duplicated today include:

- `schema = htdt.equipment.catalog-snapshot`;
- `schema_version = 1`;
- `authority_version = o100c-equipment-definition-1`;
- `definition_id`;
- `version`;
- `semantic_sha256`;
- `identity_kind`;
- nullable manufacturer/model/user_label fields.

There is already some validation asymmetry: HTDT constrains `identity_kind` to the closed backend vocabulary while Capture currently represents it as a general String in the decoded entry model.

A future backend field rename/version change or Capture decoder change can therefore make #340's production export unusable without either repository's local tests detecting it.

## Proposed change

Add one immutable cross-repository equipment-catalog compatibility fixture and CI contract.

Recommended shape:

1. create a small canonical HTDT EquipmentDefinition set containing:
   - manufacturer identity;
   - user-defined identity;
   - nullable optional fields;
   - Unicode/NFC-safe display metadata;
2. generate the exact snapshot bytes with the real HTDT model/export path;
3. pin those bytes and their SHA-256 as the v1 compatibility fixture;
4. make HTDT-Capture decode that exact fixture and verify every exact ID/version/hash tuple;
5. make HTDT verify deterministic regeneration of the same canonical bytes;
6. include negative/version fixtures for unsupported schema/authority versions;
7. require explicit contract/version change when either side intentionally changes the wire format.

Prefer an immutable pinned fixture revision rather than copying equivalent hand-authored JSON into two test suites.

## Acceptance criteria

- exact bytes generated by HTDT's production snapshot model decode successfully in HTDT-Capture;
- Capture resolves the exact ID/version/semantic-SHA tuple from those bytes;
- deterministic HTDT regeneration matches the pinned fixture hash;
- unsupported schema/authority versions fail explicitly;
- a deliberate wire-contract change requires updating a pinned compatibility version/fixture;
- CI catches a unilateral field rename/type/nullability change in either repository;
- this remains separate from Capture ingestion-plan CI because the direction and wire contract are different;
- no RDC is required.

