## Finding

Static review of current HTDT `main` (`9e6066259ec58c093e9a7587550ccf907f28402f`) found that the Capture semantic-promotion path is single-ARMeshAnchor only, while real ARKit room reconstruction is represented as multiple mesh anchors.

Current flow is explicitly:

```text
select exact RawVisualMesh binding
-> compose one T_world_from_mesh_anchor
-> convert one RawVisualMesh
-> write SceneDocument.r120_semantic_geometry
```

`CaptureSemanticPromotionRequest` names exactly one `raw_mesh_binding_id`, and `promote()` converts exactly that binding.

The resulting SceneRevision is created with:

```python
r120_semantic_geometry = geometry
```

so the document has one semantic-geometry authority for that promotion.

The test fixture also contains exactly one mesh anchor/binding.

## Why this matters

A Capture revision can legitimately contain many `ARMeshAnchor` geometry chunks in the same `coordinate_space_id`.

With the current production shape there is no defined operation that turns **all selected anchors of one capture** into one coherent room-level `SemanticAcousticGeometry`.

Promoting anchors independently is not sufficient:

- each promotion converts one local mesh under its own `T_world_from_mesh_anchor`;
- the SceneDocument field is replaced by one resulting geometry rather than accumulated composition;
- triangle/surface identities and diagnostics are defined per source raw mesh;
- duplicate/overlapping anchor geometry needs an explicit policy;
- boundary/watertightness diagnostics that only make sense after room-level composition cannot be evaluated correctly from one chunk;
- a real room may therefore appear partially imported even though every source mesh binding was successfully ingested.

This is separate from #343/#345, which concern ingestion integrity, and from #347, which concerns world-to-scene alignment.

## Proposed change

Add a deterministic, provenance-preserving **multi-anchor Capture mesh composition** boundary before semantic room promotion.

At minimum:

1. select an explicit set of raw mesh bindings from one ingestion lineage;
2. require each binding to resolve to the intended Capture coordinate-space authority, or require explicit alignment authority for any cross-space composition;
3. apply each exact `T_world_from_mesh_anchor`;
4. compose the selected chunks into one derived room-level raw/semantic source without mutating canonical Capture evidence;
5. namespace/remap vertex/triangle IDs deterministically so provenance back to `raw_visual_mesh_handoff_id` + source primitive remains exact;
6. define duplicate/overlap handling explicitly instead of silently welding or dropping geometry;
7. run diagnostics on the composed room-level result as well as retaining per-anchor diagnostics;
8. allow semantic surface assignments to reference the composed deterministic triangle identities;
9. persist the exact selected binding set, transforms, composition profile/version and resulting semantic hash;
10. promote the composed geometry atomically to one SceneRevision.

Do not infer wall/material/portal semantics merely because meshes were composed.

## Acceptance criteria

- fixture with 2+ mesh anchors in the same coordinate space produces one deterministic composed geometry;
- changing selected anchor set changes the composition identity;
- anchor-local transforms are applied exactly;
- every composed triangle remains traceable to its exact Capture handoff/source primitive;
- repeated composition of identical inputs is idempotent;
- overlapping chunks follow an explicit versioned policy and are never silently nondeterministic;
- incompatible coordinate spaces fail closed without an explicit alignment authority;
- room-level diagnostics operate on the complete selected geometry;
- promotion does not overwrite a prior anchor with another anchor while pretending the room is complete;
- repository-native tests cover the multi-anchor path; no RDC is required.

